e":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:5a84ed5df6a8463dfb5935ed5d14c88c5814ffe1fa95dfc3296ecc77ba8bdbcf","file":"preprints/Finite-angular-cylinder-covers-below-the-half-area-bound-September-27-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":32,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"48a6292c18b5111ea5ef7e869accdcec530ae57ca2c443de84c3e60ca517578b","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Finite-angular-cylinder-covers-below-the-half-area-bound-September-27-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:5a84ed5df6a8463dfb5935ed5d14c88c5814ffe1fa95dfc3296ecc77ba8bdbcf","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Finite-angular-cylinder-covers-below-the-half-area-bound-September-27-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L32"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:counterexample}\nThe tetrahedron \\eqref{eq:tetrahedron} has $A_{\\min}(K)=\\sqrt2$.\nFor every $0<\\eps\\le1/2000$, it admits a covering by\n$m=2\\lceil2/\\eps^2\\rceil$ cylinders with compact triangular perpendicular\nbases such that\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:main-asymptotic}\n \\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\sum_{i=1}^m|B_i|\n =\\frac12-\\frac{13}{6000}\\eps^2+O(\\eps^4).\n\\end{equation}\nThe remainder has absolute value at most $2\\eps^4$, and the total base\narea is strictly less than $A_{\\min}(K)/2$."}
